Null hypothesis (H_0): g and d are independent.

Alternative hypothesis (H_A): g and d are associated.

alpha level = 0.05

chi squared statistic = 4.0

degrees of freedom = 1

p value = 0.046

Assuming the null hypothesis is true (g and d are independent), there is approximately a 0.046 probability of obtaining a sample statistic equal to or less than the one observed in our sample purely by chance.

Since the p-value is less than the alpha level, we reject the null hypothesis and conclude that the alternate hypothesis (g and d are associated) is true.
